00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,070
Listen to a short talk on history.

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:02,775
OK.

3
00:00:02,775 --> 00:00:06,280
Since we’ve been talking about mechanics and then we still have a few minutes.

4
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:09,255
Let me tell you a little about the ancient Greeks

5
00:00:09,255 --> 00:00:11,040
and what they thought about mechanics.

6
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:14,658
They came up with a system that for them seem to describe

7
00:00:14,658 --> 00:00:17,070
and explain the different motions of different materials.

8
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:22,873
More than 2000 years ago, Aristotle, the ancient Greek philosopher, assumed that all the

9
00:00:22,873 --> 00:00:29,090
matter on earth were made up of four prime substances, earth, water, air and fire.

10
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:33,774
Under this system, earth is the densest, water is the next, air is less

11
00:00:33,774 --> 00:00:34,778
dense than water,

12
00:00:34,778 --> 00:00:37,120
and fire is least dense of all.

13
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:40,028
The heaviest object was made of earth and water,

14
00:00:40,028 --> 00:00:43,260
and lighter object contains significant amounts of fire or air.

15
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:48,100
So when Aristotle observed that different types of matter had different characteristics.

16
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:52,646
He assumed this was because the different types of matter were composed of different

17
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:54,270
amounts of four primary substances.

18
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:59,121
And Aristotle believes that the motions of objects could also be explained by the

19
00:00:59,121 --> 00:01:01,200
basic natures of four primary substances.

20
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:05,230
Hum, for example, there was a basic motion of up or down.

21
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:10,190
Aristotle noticed that when he released most objects, they would drop downwards.

22
00:01:10,190 --> 00:01:14,000
But he also knew that something would rise upwards, like smoke.

23
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,744
Aristotle considered an object downward or upward motion to be the result of dominant

24
00:01:18,744 --> 00:01:20,100
nature of the object.

25
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:24,688
So according to Aristotle, matter like rock were primarily composed of earth, therefore, they

26
00:01:24,688 --> 00:01:27,966
naturally want to move toward the center of the earth

27
00:01:27,966 --> 00:01:30,260
because this was all thing earthly rested.

28
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:33,260
But fire had a different resting place, the sky.

29
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:38,541
So smoke would naturally rise when it was released because it was driving toward

30
00:01:38,541 --> 00:01:40,050
its natural resting place.
